# Per-function line budgets — the large-function ratchet.
#
# Generated and maintained by `just sizes-bless`; enforced by
# `just lint-sizes` (tools/fq-lint) in the Code quality CI job.
#
# Measured from the `fn` keyword to the closing brace, so a function is
# never charged for its own doc comment. Test functions are out of scope,
# matching the file gate's exclusion of test code.
#
# Keys are `path::scope::name`, not line numbers — line numbers move on
# every edit above them, and a baseline that churned on unrelated changes
# would be ignored within a week.
#
# Every function here exceeds the 250-line cap and is pinned at its size
# when the ratchet landed. These numbers may only ever go DOWN. Lowering
# one is automatic (`just sizes-bless`); raising one, or admitting a new
# function, means hand-editing this file so a human sees it in the diff.
#
# clippy::too_many_lines is the complementary threshold gate (it counts
# CODE lines, skipping comments and blanks) — tracked in #392.
# The daemon loop, relocated by the fq/fqd split. These are the same
# lines that sat in fq-cli's `run_daemon` at 929 — moved to their own
# crate, not written here. Splitting one 929-line function across the
# assemble/run seam gives two functions, not two short ones: every value
# the assembly produces flows forward into the running half, so both
# candidate cut points measured ~26 fields wide. The struct that carries
# them across is why the two halves together exceed the original.
#
# Decomposing this properly means designing the daemon's boot sequence,
# which is #78's work and wants its own review. Admitted by hand, per
# the rule above, so that choice is visible rather than blessed.
#
# `just sizes-bless` rewrites this file from the measurements and keeps
# only the header, so re-add this note after any bless — the numbers
# below survive it, the reason they are here does not.
#
# run_hosted 581 -> 596 (2026-08-25): the edge now binds before the
# first spawn, so no fallible step remains after one, and an early
# error can no longer skip the teardown. That costs 15 lines because
# binding and serving are now two places instead of one — the bind up
# with the other fallible work, the `tokio::spawn` down where the edge
# should start answering. Raised by hand rather than blessed, because a
# correctness fix paying for itself in length is exactly the trade a
# human should see. It strengthens the case for #78 rather than
# weakening it.
